@@ -15,3 +15,14 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Phone verification (sign-up)
+
+Sign-up checks the user's mobile number with a 6-digit SMS code before it creates the account.
+
+- `POST /api/phone-verification/send` sends the code. `POST /api/phone-verification/verify` checks it. `POST /api/register` creates the account, and it refuses until the session holds a verified number.
+- Codes are stored only as salted HMACs in the session. Each code expires after 5 minutes and allows 5 attempts. A number can request at most 5 codes per hour, with at least 30 seconds between requests.
+- The SMS ends with `@<domain> #<code>`, so the [WebOTP API](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/identity/web-apis/web-otp) can fill the code in automatically. iOS/Android keyboards can also suggest it through `autocomplete="one-time-code"`.
+- Environment variables:
+  - `TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID`, `TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN`, `TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER`: send real SMS through Twilio. If they are not set, the message is logged to the server console, and in dev mode the code is also shown in the form.
+  - `OTP_SMS_DOMAIN` (optional): the domain the SMS is bound to. It defaults to the request hostname.
